# @iron-protocol/api-client — boundary rules

A typed HTTP client built on top of `@iron-protocol/api-contract`. Used by
both `apps/web` (browser fetch w/ session cookie) and `apps/mobile` (fetch
with bearer token). Stays unaware of which transport it is using.

## Imports allowed
- `@iron-protocol/api-contract`
- Standard `fetch` (assumed available — Node 18+, browsers, RN).

## Imports forbidden
- `@iron-protocol/db`, `@iron-protocol/core-logic`, `@iron-protocol/integrations`
- Anything from `apps/*`
- Cookie-jar / browser-storage code (the consumer wires that into `fetchImpl`
  or `getAuthToken`).

## Conventions
- One factory: `createApiClient({ baseUrl, getAuthToken?, fetchImpl? })`.
- Errors are thrown as `ApiError` with `.status` and `.body`.
- No retries, no caching, no request dedup. Consumers add those.
